Z||000000||KRMFiero||05-10-2001||09:28 PM||||Okay, our fire department has already had a bunch of brush fires, so we dug out one of the old pumps we have, it wasnt running 10 years ago when put away, it just didnt start up but still turned over so they stoped using it... so i took it home and it is sitting in my garage, it is the old military flat head 4 cly jeep engine.<BR>here is my question:<BR>What should i do to it to get it to run before i try to? what are some things that could of went wrong, where can i get parts for it?<BR>please help<BR>Kyle <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||05-11-2001||07:33 AM||||It's been a few years but, JC Whitney probably has some parts.<P>Start out with the obvious, plugs,wires,cap,points(make sure you check the gap too) The carb is probably going to need a good going over too.<P>Don't know what else to tell you.<BR>Good Luck<BR>Jeff<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||05-11-2001||09:23 PM||||wow, it started after 12 years this is what  i did:<P>put new oil in it<BR>put new plugs/put mistery oil in cylders<BR>quick spray of starting fluid<BR>hit the starter button<P>started right up, i had to shut it right off cause half the bolt were out and it was blowing stuff everywhere, oil line blew apart big mess but wow i am amazed 12 years and starts right up, that what i call a reliable engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     ||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||05-11-2001||09:46 PM||||I still say that the Military should have stuck with them.||||reg||1
